# Line endings are part of correctness for anything the Linux host executes.
#
# Measured defect: the release tarball shipped every ops shell script with CRLF
# endings.  On the host bash then reads `set -euo pipefail` as an option named
# `pipefail\r` and refuses with "invalid option name", so
# production_backup_window.sh, backup_v2.sh, restore_v2.sh, monitor_v2.sh and
# production_switch_four_changes.sh were all non-functional as deployed -- a
# wrapper that silently cannot run is worse than a missing one, because the
# operator believes the backup happened.  The index was already LF; the working
# tree, which the release was packaged from, was not.  These rules make the
# checked-out form LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Workflow files are integrity-checked byte-for-byte against their registered
# SHA-256 values. Keep the committed bytes unchanged on every platform.
services/rag-api/app/visual/workflows/*.json -text
